   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, fire, injury, property damage, or emergency responder attendance to the relevant regulator within 5 calendar days of learning of it. Incidents involving death, serious injury, or an active hazard must be reported within 24 hours.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, fire, injury, property damage, or emergency responder attendance to the relevant regulator within 5 calendar days of learning of it. Incidents involving death, serious injury, or an active hazard must be reported within 24 hours. The affected customer must be notified within 24 hours of a serious or active hazard, and within 5 calendar days for other reportable incidents. Reports must include known circumstances, affected model and serial number, and any immediate safety actions; manufacturers must update regulators and affected customers when material facts change."
  },
