   "rule_summary": "The maximum permitted failure rate is 8% of tested units per model. Before purchase, customers must receive the model’s per-model failure rate, material safety limitations, and any required corrective actions.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: permanent_limit_pct",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C under a common regulator-approved protocol before sale and after a material design or manufacturing change. The maximum permitted failure rate is 8% of tested units per model. Manufacturers must submit per-model test methods, sample sizes, and full results to regulators for confidential review. Before purchase, customers must receive the model’s per-model failure rate, material safety limitations, and any required corrective actions. Models exceeding a 5% failure rate must submit a regulator-approved corrective-action plan within 90 days and provide progress reports at least every 6 months; regulators may require interim safeguards or suspend sales if safety risks warrant. Any model introduced after adoption must meet the 8% limit before sale."
  },
