 "judge_section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed bag: S1 and S5 are relatively strict, S2 and S3 are weakened to Northwind's advantage, and S4 is acceptable. S2 sets an 8% permanent failure-rate ceiling with a 5% corrective-action trigger and customer-facing per-model rates, letting Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) stay on the market while meeting Halcyon's customer-disclosure red line. S3 gives new units a 24-month shut-off deadline and a 6-year retrofit with a feasibility escape, and S5 mandates recall at 8/100k but lacks a serious-injury clause, which would recall Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) and not Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4).",
